  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Nehal Ahmed Niyaz Ahmed Shaikh And Anr vs The State Of Maharashtra on 7 August, 2021 Author: M.S.Karnik Bench: M. S.Karnik 17. a Urmila Ingale Digitally In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction signed by Urmila Urmila Pramod Pramod Ingale Date: Ingale 2021.08.09 17:30:41 +0530 Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2547 Of 2019 Nehal Ahmed Niyaz Ahmed Shaikh and anr. .... Applicants Vs. State of Maharashtra ..... Respondent Mr.Marmik Shaikh i/b Mr.Kushal Mor, for the Applicants. Smt. P.N. Dabholkar, App for the Respondent - State. Mr.D.M. Lokhande, Psi, Bhoiwada Police Station, Bhiwandi present. Coram : M. S.Karnik, J. Date : 07th August, 2021 P.C. : .",
    "facts": "1 are seeking pre-arrest bail in C.R. No. I - 284 of 2019 re with Bhiwandi Police Station, Thane for the ofences punish under Sections 188, 328, 272, 273, 224 r/w 34 of Indian Pe Code and 59, 26(2), 27 of the Food Safety and Standards Ac 2006. It is alleged by frst informant Shankar Kishan Food Safety Ofcer that on receipt of confdential informati regarding sale of banned food products, he visited M/s.New Bombay Supari Kirana and General Stores. Applicant N 17. aba 2547.19.doc present in the shop. Applicant No. 1 informed the concerned ofcer that owner of the shop is Faiyyaz Ahmad Newaz Ahmad Shaikh i.e. Applicant No.2 and he was not present in the shop on that date. No banned food products was found in the shop. However, when the godown of the frst foor was checked, banned products in the nature of pan masala, tobacco, gutka total valuing Rs. 2,37,074/- was found. 2. It is the contention of the learned Counsel for the Applicant No.1 that he is a student and was only present in the shop on that day as his brother - Applicant No.2 was not in town. Applicant No.1 has no concern with the business. Applicant No.2 is the owner of the shop. This Court by interim order dated 21/11/2019 granted interim pre-arrest bail. Pursuant to the order passed by this Court, learned APP submits that applicants co-operated with the investigation. The entire stocks are already Nehal Ahmed Niyaz Ahmed Shaikh And Anr vs The State Of Maharashtra on 7 August, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/67741651/ 2 seized. It is further pointed out that even charge-sheet is fled on 31/03/2021 in Session Case No. 626/21 before the trial Court.",
